Materials
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this project I used several Raspberry Pi Pico W boards and standard,
 low-cost electronics components such as buttons,
 potentiometers,
 and LEDs.
 A separate WiFi router was an additional necessary component,
 since DuqNet does not allow ad-hoc UDP .
 The idea was to build a simple wireless OSC controller that transmitted data to a Max/MSP patch running on a Macintosh computer,
